Background
After MSSQL → PostgreSQL DB schema conversion completes (Job 2), the Java or C# application code requires targeted changes to remain compatible with the transformed PostgreSQL database. These changes are driven by the dependency rules applied during scanning and the findings stored in Db-dependency/Java-MSSQL-dependency.json (for Java apps) or Db-dependency/CSharp-MSSQL-dependency.json (for C# apps).

Job 3 reads those findings, applies remediations from the appropriate language-specific Remediation KB — Java-MSSQL Remediation KB or C#-MSSQL Remediation KB — and produces a modified codebase with a post-transformation report and a separate GitHub commit.

For M-Basic and M-Container-Mono pathways, additional configuration file and infrastructure-level changes are required beyond violation remediations to ensure the containerised/cloud-ready application connects correctly to the transformed PostgreSQL database.

Note — Per-file breakdown in the Dependency Resolution Plan screen is not required. The same UX as the M-Basic app modernization flow applies: total violations and per-violation summary only, no per-file breakdown.

